/***********************************************************************

	rt_auto_relight.mtr

	Light material used only to give auto-relight's engine-synthesized
	lights (vk_auto_relight.cpp AR5, docs/plans/auto_relight.md) a distinct,
	greppable name instead of the generic lights/defaultPointLight every
	other shader-less point light falls back to. Debug tools that print
	lightShader->GetName() -- r_rtGILightDump, r_showLights, the auto-relight
	console table -- can then identify a synthesized light at a glance.

	Deliberately byte-identical to lights/defaultPointLight (materials/lights.mtr)
	otherwise: same falloff image, same stage. This changes nothing about how
	the light looks, only what it's called.

***********************************************************************/

lights/rtAutoRelight
{
	lightFalloffImage	makeintensity( lights/squarelight1a.tga )
	{
		forceHighQuality
		map lights/squarelight1.tga
		colored
		zeroClamp
	}
}
